                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9315 Manchuria/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-13">October 13, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        13—12:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>454. According to an official Tass report in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pravda</hi> October 13th Japanese Manchurian divisions crossed the Soviet
                    frontier on 6th, 8th, and 12th of October and fired on Soviet border guards.
                    Skirmish on October 12th included rifle and machine-gun fire and casualties
                    reported. The Soviet Government has protested to Tokyo and has proposed naming a
                    mixed commission for investigation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
